# Edge caching & ISR — production contract

Tenant data is **not** a CDN document. If you cache it at the edge without
an org tag, you will leak workspace A into workspace B. Read the whitepaper
`enterprise-bundle/whitepapers/Multi-Tenant-Caching-Architecture.md`
before adding `revalidate`, `unstable_cache`, or `fetch` cache options.

## What may be cached

| Surface | Cache? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Landing (`/`) | yes | Public marketing. ISR / `revalidate` OK. |
| Static assets (`_next/static`) | yes | Immutable hashes. |
| `/api/health` | **no** | Already `Cache-Control: no-store`. |
| `/dashboard`, `/settings/*`, `/agents` | **no** | Cookie-authenticated. `force-dynamic`. |
| `/demo/*` | short / private | Public mock, but still no user PII. |
| Stripe / Lemon webhooks | **never** | `force-dynamic`, raw body. |
| `GET /api/stripe/portal` | n/a | POST only. |

## Next.js 16 rules

- Authenticated segments: `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"` on the
  layout (`app/(app)/layout.tsx` already). Do not add `revalidate = 60`
  there.
- `fetch` from a Server Component to your own origin: default to
  `cache: "no-store"` when the request would include cookies.
- `unstable_cache` / `"use cache"` keys **must** include `organizationId`
  (and usually `userId`) derived from `requireUser()`, never from a query
  string the client controls.
- `revalidateTag` / `revalidatePath` after billing webhooks if you ever
  cache plan entitlements. Tag format: `org:{organizationId}:billing`.
  Never a global `revalidatePath("/")` to “fix” tenant data.
- ISR (`revalidate: 3600`) is for **public** pages only.

## Edge / CDN

- Vercel: `regions` in `vercel.json` may pin `iad1`. Do not enable
  full-route CDN cache for `(app)` just to chase TTFB.
- `proxy.ts` runs on the edge. Keep it tiny: session refresh + redirect.
  No Stripe, no model, no admin client.
- `Cache-Control: private, no-store` on any response that used
  `cookies()` or `requireUser()`.
- `s-maxage` is for public marketing HTML/JSON only.
- Purge by **tag**, not by wildcard URL, when the tag is org-scoped.

## Audit checklist (run before launch)

1. `curl -I` dashboard with no cookie → 307/302 to login, not 200 HTML
   of someone else’s shell.
2. Two orgs, two sessions: response bodies never contain the other org’s
   `stripe_customer_id` or billing email.
3. Webhook POST is uncached (second POST with same body still hits Node).
4. Landing `Age` / `x-vercel-cache` may be HIT; `/settings/billing` must
   not.
5. No `Cache-Control: public` on `Set-Cookie` responses.

If a cache layer cannot speak org tags, **do not cache the route**.
